-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",303,{
[9665]="70036FDB\n1\tTalk to Dudsig in Oserley\tDudsig is near the stable in Oserley. Thane Ordlac instructed you to speak with Dudsig, his chief captain, and learn what aid can be given to Oserley while he musters his meagre garrison.\n2\tCollect stolen goods (total: 5)\tThe brigands' camp is in the fields west of Oserley. Dudsig has asked you to recover stolen goods from the brigands who have stolen from the people of Oserley.\n3\tBring the stolen goods to Dudsig in Oserley\tDudsig is near the stable in Oserley, east of the brigands' camp. You should bring the stolen goods back to Dudsig.\n",
[9666]="7005F868\n1\tFollow the thoroughfare through Gloomingtarn and meet Spall and Hersegg at Lugun-nâla\tLugun-nâla, the span that crosses Durthuzâram to Abkân'aban, the Stone of Wakening, can be found to the north of Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Hermáth Stormhammer has informed you that Spall and Hersegg have gone north to Lugun-nâla with his warriors. You should travel to Lugun-nâla and meet Spall and Hersegg.\n2\tTalk to Spall at Lugun-nâla\tSpall can be found at Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn. You have arrived at Lugun-nâla. You should talk to Spall.\n3\tTalk to Hersegg at Lugun-nâla\tHersegg can be found at Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn. After arriving at Lugun-nâla, Spall has informed you that Hersegg wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Hersegg.\n4\tScout the Iron Crown encampment on the western banks of Durthuzâram\030Find and collect an Iron Crown scroll-case\tThe Iron Crown encampment can be found to the north of Lugun-nâla, along the banks of Durthuzâram. Hersegg has asked you to scout the Iron Crown encampment along the western bank of Durthuzâram and recover a scroll-case if you find one among the Iron Crown.\n5\tDeliver the Iron Crown scroll-case to Hersegg at Lugun-nâla\tHersegg can be found at Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn. You have explored the Iron Crown encampment at Durthuzâram and recovered a scroll-case. You should return to Hersegg.\n",
[9667]="700223AB\n1\tDefeat pale-folk pillagers (total: 10)\030Defeat pale-folk blades (total: 10)\tThe Pale-folk pillagers and blades can be found throughout the Library of Tham Mirdaín.\n",
[9668]="7000AE1A\n1\tReturn the heartwood to Sergeant-at-Arms Caddfrith at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect heartwood\tLeafcull Huorns can be found in the Grimwood Forest, south-west of Tol Ascarnen. Sergeant-at-Arms Caddafrith has asked you to assist her in crafting a horn to call forces to fight against Angmar's army when they assail Tol Ascarnen. To complete the stand, she needs a heartwood from the Leafcull Huorns. She suggests you take allies, for the Huorns are a dangerous foe.\n",
[9669]="7001D17F\n1\tLocate the northern ancient pillar\030Locate the central ancient pillar\030Locate the southern ancient pillar\tThe ancient pillars can be located among the ruins of Sâd Doldúr, which can be found by following the path below, down the mountain until you reach the ruins proper. There are three pillars, located in the northern, central, and southern portions of the ruins. The cairn stones located among the ruins appear to be resistant to the blight that is sweeping the area. Himeinior asked you to travel to each of these locations and examine the pillars.\n2\tTalk to Himeinior near Barad Angol\tHimeinior is at the camp near Barad Angol upon the hill, north of the pillars. After examining the ancient pillars, you did not see any sign of corruption or taint. Return to Barad Angol and report this to Himeinior.\n",
[9670]="7002658B\n1\tRead the names etched in the pillars (total: 7)\tOrchalwë has asked you to read the names etched into the pillars.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë wants to speak with you about the etched pillars.\n",
[9671]="7004E92C\n1\tDestroy the unnatural ice (total: 12)\tYou should destroy any unnatural ice formations that you find on the Withered Heath.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed unnatural ice formations.\n",
[9672]="70066911\n1\tCatch fat fish (total: 2)\tMadern has invited you to participate in a fishing contest. Catch two fish in as many minutes while standing near the designated marker. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Madern\tYou have caught two fish within the time limit. Talk to Madern on the road between the farm, Wetcroft, and the western bank of Nen Eilen.\n",
[9673]="7006691D\n1\tCatch the legendary fish\tMadern has challenged you to catch a beast of a fish along the north-western banks of Pinnath Gelin near a scarecrow. Catch the mysterious fish.\n2\tTalk to Madern\tYou have caught an impressive fish. Talk to Madern on the road between the farm, Wetcroft, and the western bank of Nen Eilen.\n",
[9674]="7006691E\n1\tEarn points (total: 5)\tThe farmer Madern hosts a fishing contest on the western bank of Nen Eilen. 'The fish at the lone banner are eager to bite but are worth only one point. 'The fish at the spot marked by two banners are a bit more shy but are worth two points apiece. 'The fish at the spot marked by three banners are not so easily persuaded to take any sort of bait, but a fish caught there is worth three points! Catch five points worth of fish in three minutes. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Madern\tYou have caught enough points' worth of fish within the time limit. Talk to Madern on the road between the farm, Wetcroft, and the western bank of Nen Eilen.\n",
[9675]="70007583\n1\tBring the pipe-weed to Roger Hawkling\tRoger Hawkling can be found at Adso Haybank's camp along the Great East Road, west of Bree, north of the Old Forest. Stoutthrush wants you to bring the cask of pipe-weed to Roger Hawkling.\n",
[9676]="700494C1\n1\tTalk to Párgrub\tYou should talk to Párgrub.\n2\tTalk to Párgrub\tPárgrub can be found near Thorzhaf. You should speak with Párgrub about the match.\n",
[9677]="7005A497\n1\tCollect pine tree resin (total: 10)\tResin can be found on pine trees in the forests in western Azanulbizar. You should gather pine tree resin.\n2\tTalk to Dráttur in Zirakazhâr\tDráttur is located in Zirakazhâr. Bring the pine tree resin to Dráttur.\n3\tFill the cauldron with resin\tThe cauldron is located in Zirakazhâr. You should put the resin into the cauldron.\n4\tPick up the resin-filled bucket\tThe pitch-filled bucket can be found in Zirakazhâr. Collect the pitch-filled bucket.\n5\tFill the pitch cauldrons (total: 4)\tPitch cauldrons can be found along the walls of Zirakazhâr. You should fill the pitch cauldrons.\n6\tTalk to Dráttur in Amdân.\tDráttur is located in Amdân. Return to Dráttur.\n",
[9678]="7002BBDB\n1\tDefeat Fúshbraf\030Defeat Ironarm\tEnd Saruman's experiments by defeating both the leader of the Abominations and the leader of the Fire-orcs.\n",
[9679]="7002BBD7\n1\tDefeat Ironarm\tThe source of Saruman's Abominations must be destroyed at last.\n",
[9680]="7002BBDA\n1\tDefeat Fúshbraf\tDestroy Saruman's Fire-orcs before he can breed more.\n",
[9681]="70017535\n1\tAid Glorelloth: collect fungus from the Sixteenth Hall\030Aid Pentlenn: collect samples from the Sixteenth Hall\030Complete Odmar's task in the Sixteenth Hall\030Complete Ymar's task within the Sixteenth Hall\030Complete Lar's task in the Sixteenth Hall\tThe Watchers of the Sixteenth Hall are in the Shadowed Refuge in Moria. The Elves and dwarves you seek are named Lar, Ymar, Odmar, Pentlenn, and Glorelloth. Mallas has asked you to help his fellows at the Shadowed Refuge do various tasks in the Sixteenth Hall.\n2\tReturn to Mallas at the Shadowed Refuge\tThe Elf Mallas is at the Shadowed Refuge. You have completed the tasks set before you by the dwarves Ymar, Lar, and Odmar and the Elves Glorelloth and Pentlenn, and should now bring tidings to Mallas of all that has transpired.\n",
[9682]="70054671\n1\tDestroy plague cauldrons (total: 10)\tPlague cauldrons have been setup in the Circle of Madness. You should destroy plague cauldrons.\n2\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog is stationed inside Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[9683]="70001740\n1\tKill the Hillman Plague-bearer\tWithin the shadow of the Ram Dúath a Hillman Plague-bearer commands her forces south into the North Downs. You must find her and defeat her. You should find and defeat the leader of the Angmarim forces.\n2\tKill the Hillman Plague-bearer (quantity: see journal)\tWithin the shadow of the Ram Dúath a Hillman Plague-bearer commands her forces south into the North Downs. You must find her and defeat her. You should find and defeat the leader of the Angmarim forces.\n3\tCompleted\tAfter entering the Ram Dúath, you sought out and defeated the leader of the Angmarim forces.\n",
[9684]="7000C386\n1\tPlace the pike in a sturdy bit of earth\tThe stake should be placed on a sturdy patch of earth in the place where the Orcs are gathered within Goblin-town. Aeglas' plan is nearly complete. He believes that the items within the bag will drive the Orcs into a frenzy and set them upon the goblins of Goblin-town.\n2\tTalk to Aeglas in the Goblin-town prison\tAeglas is in his cell within the Goblin-town prison. After placing the Orc-head and pike in the gathering place, the Orcs grew enraged, but the goblins seemed prepared for their aggression and quickly put the matter to end. You should return to Aeglas with your report.\n",
[9685]="70030890\n1\tCollect Mordor Orc War-plans (total: 3)\tAssault-plans can be found in the Orc-encampment of Nîn-stazg. You should collect the Orcs' plans so that Floodwend may be prepared for an attack.\n2\tBring the war-plans to Thane Radwig\tThane Radwig is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend, preparing his town for an impending attack. You should bring the war-plans you gathered to Radwig.\n",
[9686]="70015E2E\n1\tPlant seeds (total: 8)\tThere are clearings throughout Glâd Ereg, the forest south of Gwingris. Celebrandir instructed you to plant the seeds in clear spaces where the trees will have room to grow.\n2\tTalk to Celebrandir at Gwingris\tCelebrandir is at Gwingris, north of Glâd Ereg. You should return to Celebrandir and let him know that you have planted the seeds as he requested.\n",
[9687]="70025EEC\n1\tCollect flowers (total: 5)\tFlowers can be found around the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow asked you to gather up flowers from around the farm.\n2\tThe planters are at the market-grounds. The flowers need to be placed in the planters.\t\n3\tTalk to Milo Longfurrow\tMilo Longfurrow is at the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow will be pleased to hear the flowers have been planted.\n",
[9688]="70025ED4\n1\tCollect scarecrows (total: 6)\tThe scarecrows are behind a farm-house to the east. The scarecrows must be collected before they can be placed in the fields.\n2\tThe scarecrows should be placed in the fields around the Northcotton Farm. The hobbit-children will delight in seeing the scarecrows in the fields.\t\n3\tTalk to Milo Longfurrow\tMilo Longfurrow is at the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow will be pleased to hear that the scarecrows are placed.\n",
[9689]="70009D5B\n1\tPlant the seeds Amabel gave you in her special field\tThe field is next to Amabel near the Party Tree in the Shire. Amabel has asked you to plant some very special seeds in her field near the Party Tree. She would like you to prove that you have the true patience of a farmer. Hint: This is a crafting quest. Use the Crafting Panel to execute the recipe you have been given.\n2\tTalk to Amabel Redfern\030Collect Empty Spore Pouch\tAmabel Redfern is near the Party Tree in the Shire. You should return the empty bag of seeds to Amabel Redfern so that she knows you have planted the seeds as asked.\n",
[9690]="70002EFE\n1\tReturn the mining-records to Regin\030Collect the mining-records\tThe lost mining records are somewhere around Othrikar, probably in a chest or locker. Regin has asked you to recover old mining-records that may give a clue to the location of the legendary \"father-lode\".\n",
[9691]="70049626\n1\tObtain an offering\tGhâsh-hai can be found throughout Talath Úrui. You should defeat Ghâsh-hai to obtain an offering that is an acceptable gift to treat with Borangos.\n2\tBring the offering to the Watching Stone\tThe Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth. You should bring the offering to the Watching Stone.\n3\tExplore the Path of Ember\030Explore the Path of Fire\030Explore the Path of Ash\tNargroth is located in Talath Úrui. You should explore the depths of Nargroth.\n4\tReturn to the Watching Stone\tThe Watching Stone can be found in Nargroth. You should return to the Watching Stone.\n",
[9692]="70020DC6\n1\tTalk to a hobbit at Maur Tulhau\tThe hobbit-village of Maur Tulhau lies to the north-west of Gwin Curhonon's hiding place. Gwin Curhonon asked you to bring word of his rescue to his kinsfolk in Maur Tulhau.\n",
[9693]="7000D4E7\n1\tTalk to Brúnfair\030Collect Scrap of a Dwarf Pledge\tSomeone in Gath Forthnír will surely be interested the information you uncovered. You have acquired information about Angmar's allies and plans. You should immediately inform someone of this development.\n",
[9694]="7000D4E9\n1\tTalk to Brúnfair\030Collect Scrap of a Goblin Pledge\tGath Forthnír is in the eastern reaches of Angmar, beyond Rammas Deluon. You have acquired information about Angmar's allies and plans. You should immediately inform someone at Gath Forthnír of this development.\n",
[9695]="7000D4ED\n1\tTalk to Brúnfair\030Collect Scrap of a Nomad Pledge\tGath Forthnír lies in the eastern reaches of Angmar, beyond Rammas Deluon. You have acquired information about Angmar's allies and plans. You should immediately inform someone at Gath Forthnír of this development.\n",
[9696]="7000D4F3\n1\tTalk to Brúnfair\030Collect Scrap of a Half-Orc Pledge\tGath Forthnír is in the eastern reaches of Angmar. You have acquired information about Angmar's allies and plans. You should immediately inform someone at Gath Forthnír of this development.\n",
})
